## Reference rig: BENCH place with PoE power + adopted-unit SSH (P1 pattern).
## Extreme WS-AP3915i reference unit on ap-lan4 — the fully-mechanical rig:
## every resource is machine-controlled, no human steps, safe unattended.
##
## The POWER resource is the shared exporter's NetworkPowerPort (conwrt_poe
## backend, place ap-lan4 on the coordinator); the NETWORK resource is the
## NetworkService exported with it. Acquire the remote place, then drive
## transitions: power cycle (cold-boot tests), SSH (deploys/config), or a
## net-first image-per-run campaign (labgrid/README.md).
##
## Coordinator/exporter addresses live in local bench records (gitignored);
## placeholders below.
targets:
  main:
    resources:
      RemotePlace:
        name: ap-lan4
    drivers:
      SSHDriver:
        connection_timeout: 120.0
        explicit_scp_mode: True
      # PowerDriver comes from the exporter's NetworkPowerPort via the place.
## Method gating (docs/DEVICE-TRANSITIONS.md transition table):
##   sysupgrade  [ssh-service]                -> board-name-match first
##   adopt/firstboot [ssh-service]            -> rom-audit + keys-and-password
##                                               + tftp-lifeline-armed (AGENTS.md R1)
##   tftp-boot   [power,tftp-server,...]      -> only when flash boot FAILS
##                                               (boot_net never runs otherwise)
